          Q('Use Euler’s method with Δt = 10 min to estimate T(30).', 'T(10) ≈ 140 − 9.72 = 130.28; T(20) ≈ 130.28 − 8.41 = 121.87; T(30) ≈ 121.87 − 7.27 ≈ 114.6'),
          Q('Compare with the measured 116°F. Is Euler’s estimate an over- or underestimate? Why?', 'Underestimate; the solution is concave up, so tangent lines lie below the curve.'),
